Exact-GP radial ghosts fail sooner than the reused provisional-boundary
baseline, and true gauge freezing advances rather than delays the 0.1 drift
crossing. Their combination also loses metric admissibility. Thus neither
the provisional boundary alone nor the live gauge alone explains or cures
the instability. No GL interpretation or k-scan resumption follows.
